Third-party attribution
=======================

This project is released under the zlib License; see LICENSE. That is the
same license raylib itself uses, chosen deliberately so that the original
terms carry through the example ports rather than being replaced by
something stricter.

Every file here is under that license. An earlier version carved out two
MPL 2.0 files inherited from a vendored -sys wrapper; that wrapper is gone,
replaced by the official org.jank-lang.commons/raylib-sys package, so the
carve-out went with it.

zlib asks two things of an altered version: that the origin not be
misrepresented, and that the alteration be plainly marked. This file is that
marking.


raylib
------
  Copyright (c) 2013-2026 Ramon Santamaria (@raysan5)
  https://github.com/raysan5/raylib
  Licensed under the zlib/libpng license (the same license as this project).

  raylib is not copied into this repository, and is no longer built here.
  The library comes from org.jank-lang.commons/raylib-sys on Clojars, which
  pins the same upstream commit (tag 6.0, dbc56a87).

  A git submodule (jank-raylib-sys/raylib) is still fetched, but only as the
  source of example ASSETS - the shaders, models, textures, fonts and audio
  that 101 of the examples load from raylib/examples/*/resources/, which the
  published jar does not carry. Nothing in it is compiled or patched.


raylib examples
---------------
  Copyright (c) 2013-2026 Ramon Santamaria (@raysan5) and contributors
  Licensed under the zlib/libpng license (the same license as this project).

  The example programs under raylib-examples/src/raylib_examples/ are ports
  of raylib's own example programs to jank. They are altered versions: the
  logic is reimplemented in jank, and the interop constraints described in
  docs/guide/ forced structural changes throughout. Every example's docstring
  names the upstream C source it was ported from (e.g. core/core_basic_window,
  shapes/shapes_bouncing_ball), and raylib-examples/README.md lists the same
  mapping in table form.

  One deliberate behavioural deviation from the originals, applied uniformly:
  every example sets FLAG_WINDOW_HIGHDPI.


rlights.h
---------
  Copyright (c) 2017-2024 Victor Fisac (@victorfisac) and
                          Ramon Santamaria (@raysan5)
  Licensed under the zlib/libpng license (the same license as this project).

  jank-raylib-sys/include/jank_rlights.h is an altered version of raylib's
  examples/shaders/rlights.h. CreateLight and UpdateLightValues are kept
  verbatim from the original and marked static; the surrounding index-based
  scalar wrappers and per-type uniform setters are new work, needed because
  jank functions can neither take nor return native values. The file's own
  header comment carries the same attribution.


